    Bug 1846550 - add ability to manually sort (order) folders in folder pane. r=aleca,darktrojan,freaktechnik

    Changes summary:

      - Added new property `userSortOrder` to `nsDBFolderInfo`. This property represents it's order among siblings.
      - Added new property `userSortOrder` to `nsMsgDBFolder`. This corresponds to `userSortOrder` above.
      - The existing property getter `nsMsgDBFolder::GetSortOrder` returns it if `userSortOrder` is not `NO_SORT_VALUE`, and returns a value based on the conventional rule if it is `NO_SORT_VALUE` for the backward compatibility.
      - The method to compare `sortOrder` has been changed. Previously the order was like 1, 10, 100, 2, 20 as lexical order, changed to 1, 2, 10, 20, 100 as numerical order.
      - Show folder drag indicator when dragging a folder to the edge of the target folder.
      - Set the order of the dragged folder so that it is between the order of its siblings before and after the position from which it was dropped. The order of the siblings is also incremented to ensure that this is the case.
      - This also updates the `FolderTreeRow.folderSortOrder` of the rows for the folder in the active views.
      - It then updates the position of the moved folder row in each view. This is done by comparing the `FolderTreeRow.folderSortOrder` with its sibling rows.
      - The behavior when dropping directly on the target folder is the same as before.
      - Of course, folders can only be moved within the same server.
      - Folders can only be moved to the "All Folders" view. (can be moved from other views to the "All Folders" view).

    I initially thought it would be more natural to have new subfolders to always added at the bottom, and implemented it that way. However, I accepted Betterbird's argument that the position of subfolders added to "the folder where the user has not yet manually sorted any subfolders" should be in the "natural" (alphabetical) order as before, and adopted their code that did so. No point in reinventing the wheel, so I still use that code in this patch.
    https://github.com/Betterbird/thunderbird-patches/blob/main/128/bugs/1846550-manually-sort-folders-fix-new-folder.patch
    https://github.com/Betterbird/thunderbird-patches/blob/main/128/bugs/1846550-manually-sort-folders-fix-new-folder2.patch

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D238193

